error[ffi_unknown_field]: `fixedbugs-2062-records.h` declares no `x` in `struct nested`: clang read the header, and that type has no such field
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2062-a-member-of-a-struct-a-record-holds-is-told-where-the-header-has-it.hero:12:9
     |
  12 |         x: i32  #~ ffi_unknown_field
     |         ^
  note: `x` is a member of the struct `pos` inside `struct nested`, which C reaches as `pos.x`: a group's `record` names the members the header gives its type itself (§4.19, § 13)
  note: what builds today: bind `Nested` `partial`, naming only `kind`, and end a construction of it with `rest: zero`, which leaves `pos` to C
  note: or reach `pos.x` through a function of the program's own in a header that includes `fixedbugs-2062-records.h`, `static inline int nested_x(const struct nested *t) { return t->pos.x; }`, which this group then names in `fixedbugs-2062-records.h`'s place
  note: or reach it by a macro, as C's own headers reach `s6_addr`: a header of the program's own that includes `fixedbugs-2062-records.h` and defines `#define x pos.x`, which this group then names in `fixedbugs-2062-records.h`'s place, so `x` stays a field; the macro renames every `x` read after it
